# One file per release: /etc/midwest-census/endpoint-<release>.env
#
# `midwest-serve@<release>.service` reads this before it starts the endpoint. The instance name (%i)
# already gives each release its own binary, store directory and log directory; the only thing it
# cannot derive is the port, because a port is a deployment decision, not a property of a commit.
#
# Give every release a distinct port. Two endpoints on one port is the failure this file exists to
# make impossible: the second bind fails and systemd retries it forever.
CENSUS_LISTEN=127.0.0.1:9080

# After starting a release on its own port, register it with the node explicitly:
#
#   curl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:19095/deployments \
#     -H 'content-type: application/json' \
#     -d '{"uri":"http://127.0.0.1:9081/"}'
#
# The node then has two deployments of the same origin, and both are visible in
# `curl http://127.0.0.1:19095/deployments`. Retire the old one by stopping its instance; the node
# stops redelivering to it, and the new release keeps serving the same journal.
